# Implementation Plan - WhatsApp Student Helpdesk Assistant (HOD)

Production-grade TypeScript/Node.js backend service for the **WhatsApp Student Helpdesk Assistant for the Head of Department (HOD)**, powered by **PostgreSQL** and equipped with an official **Meta WhatsApp Cloud API Integration Layer** and a complete **DevOps production toolkit**.

---

## The WhatsApp Integration Layer (`src/adapters/whatsapp/`)

The WhatsApp layer connects the backend service with Meta's WhatsApp Cloud API (or authorized Business Solution Providers like Twilio/Infobip/Gupshup). It handles inbound webhooks, security verification, message normalization, and outbound messaging.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Student as Student (WhatsApp)
    participant Meta as Meta WhatsApp Cloud API
    participant WH as Webhook Route (POST /webhooks/whatsapp)
    participant Sig as Signature Validator (HMAC SHA-256)
    participant Norm as Message Normalizer
    participant Orch as Conversation Orchestrator
    participant Client as WhatsApp Graph API Client

    Student->>Meta: Sends WhatsApp message ("Need bonafide certificate")
    Meta->>WH: POST /webhooks/whatsapp (Payload + X-Hub-Signature-256)
    WH->>Sig: Verify X-Hub-Signature-256 with WHATSAPP_APP_SECRET
    Sig-->>WH: Signature OK
    WH-->>Meta: 200 OK (immediate acknowledgment < 3s)
    WH->>Norm: Parse raw Meta payload
    Norm->>Orch: Normalized Message (from, msg_id, text, timestamp)
    Orch->>Orch: Process via State Machine & Classifier
    Orch->>Client: Send Reply (Text / Interactive Form Link)
    Client->>Meta: POST https://graph.facebook.com/v20.0/{PHONE_NUMBER_ID}/messages
    Meta->>Student: WhatsApp reply delivered with Google Form link
```

### Components of the WhatsApp Layer:

1. **Webhook Verification & Security (`src/adapters/whatsapp/signature.ts`)**:
   - `GET /webhooks/whatsapp`: Responds to Meta's initial handshake (`hub.mode === 'subscribe'` and `hub.verify_token`).
   - `POST /webhooks/whatsapp`: Validates the `X-Hub-Signature-256` HTTP header against the raw body buffer using the app's secret key (`crypto.createHmac('sha256', APP_SECRET)`).

2. **Inbound Message Normalizer (`src/adapters/whatsapp/normalizer.ts`)**:
   - Unpacks Meta's nested payload structure (`entry[].changes[].value.messages[]`).
   - Extracts:
     - Sender phone number (`from`)
     - Unique provider message ID (`id`) for database idempotency
     - Message timestamp (`timestamp`)
     - Message content (text message body, interactive button reply ID, or quick reply)

3. **Outbound WhatsApp Client (`src/adapters/whatsapp/client.ts`)**:
   - Sends outbound messages through the official Meta Graph API:
     - Text messages (FAQ answers, office hours, safety disclosures).
     - Interactive button messages (category quick-pick: *"Certificates"*, *"Leave"*, *"Attendance"*, *"Appointments"*).
     - CTA URL messages (direct clickable Google Form link buttons).
   - Handles Bearer token authentication (`WHATSAPP_API_TOKEN`) and Phone Number ID (`WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID`).
   - Includes retry logic with exponential backoff for transient network issues.

4. **Local WhatsApp Simulator (`src/simulator/cli.ts` & `src/simulator/mock-client.ts`)**:
   - Enables full end-to-end testing of the WhatsApp conversation flow locally in terminal without requiring a live Meta developer account during development.

